  "interpretation": [
    "Training uses a distinct Walker epoch; packet evaluation uses the exact frozen baseline config, trace hash, and deterministic flows.",
    "Training returns and losses are diagnostic, not substitutes for packet performance metrics.",
    "Results are provisional; five seeds do not establish statistical significance or generalization.",
    "When enabled, WAIT advances one topology sample. Training masks it when no future contact-graph route exists; packet evaluation additionally requires that the planned route fit the remaining packet deadline.",
    "The no-WAIT ablation evaluates the same trained weights with WAIT disabled; it is an inference-time action-mask ablation, not a separately trained policy.",
    "WAIT reward is normalized by full trace duration only when reward.normalize_wait_penalty_by_horizon is true; the default preserves the sample-normalized Phase 4.1 reward.",
    "No fuzzy clustering or federated learning is included."
  ],
